GCab Release Notes

This document describes the public release workflow. Local development may
use jj; the release commit, tag and push are done through git.

Note: if your working copy is a jj-colocated checkout, do not run git commit
or git tag against jj's detached HEAD. Use a normal git clone for the release,
or make sure the final release commit has already been exported to git.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Prepare the release

   - Update NEWS at your discretion before making the release commit.

   - Update the project version in meson.build to the new release version.

   - Make sure the release commit is the intended final commit and that the
     working tree is clean:

       git status --short

2. Build and test from a clean tree

       meson setup _build .
       meson compile -C _build
       meson test -C _build --print-errorlogs

   Optionally verify the release tarball builds and tests successfully:

       meson dist -C _build
       tar -xf _build/meson-dist/gcab-<version>.tar.xz -C /tmp
       cd /tmp/gcab-<version>
       meson setup _dist-build .
       meson compile -C _dist-build
       meson test -C _dist-build --print-errorlogs

3. Commit and push the release commit

   Set the release version and tag:

       export release_version="1.7"
       export release_tag="${release_version}"

   The version must match meson.build. The tag must be the bare version
   number, without a "v" prefix, because GNOME's release service expects the
   tarball to be named gcab-${release_tag}.tar.xz.

   Stage only the intended release files (include NEWS if you updated it):

       git add meson.build NEWS
       git commit -m "Release ${release_version}"
       git push origin HEAD

4. Create and push the signed tag

   Follow the GNOME handbook. Preferred, if git-evtag is available:

       git evtag sign "${release_tag}"

   Fallback:

       git tag -s -m "GCab ${release_version}" "${release_tag}"

   Then push the tag:

       git push origin "${release_tag}"

   Do not use "git tag -f" for a final release tag. Do not prefix the tag with
   "v": the release tarball must remain gcab-${release_tag}.tar.xz.

5. Release service (normal path)

   The .gitlab-ci.yml pipeline includes the GNOME release-service. On a
   protected release tag it:

   - uses the tarball produced by the configured dist job ("build-gnomeos"),
   - uploads the tarball and its sha256sum to download.gnome.org,
   - creates the GitLab release from the tag message.

   GNOME protects tags in the GNOME group automatically; ensure the tag was
   accepted as protected, then monitor the pipeline until the release-service
   job succeeds.

   No manual upload is needed when the release service is available.
